Stubs that keep the URLs the Japanese posts had before English became the
default language, when they lived at the site root rather than under /ja/.

GitHub Pages serves static files only and cannot return a 301, and
jekyll-redirect-from is no help here: lang-exclusive drops each Japanese post
from the English build entirely, so the plugin never sees the document that
would carry the redirect. Each stub is therefore its own page, claiming the old
permalink and marked lang-exclusive: ["en"] so it is written to the root and not
duplicated under /ja/.

Generated from the URLs Jekyll itself produced. The five posts that have an
English translation are not listed: their old Japanese URL is now the English
post's URL, so a stub there would collide.
